Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Complex-contour S/R split: first and second order (toy model)\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"cc87e8ae-e3b5-4ade-9fe5-a9a2958e1713"],

Cell["\<\
Flat 3D Poisson toy model of the complex-contour regularisation project (A. \
Spiers). Specification: Claude Implementation/singular-field-consistency.tex. \
All functions live in ContourSecondOrder.wl in this folder; the .wls scripts \
are the pass/fail test versions of the sections below. Conventions: Y_l = \
Y_l0 orthonormal, [f]_l = Sqrt[Pi(2l+1)] Integrate[f P_l(mu), {mu,-1,1}], L_l \
psi = psi'' + 2 psi'/r - l(l+1) psi/r^2, unit-strength first-order mode \
source delta(r-r0), kappa_l = -(q/r0^2) Sqrt[4 Pi (2l+1)], H(z) = 1 + (I/Pi) \
Log[z-r0], deltaExt = I/(Pi (z-r0)); real-axis values are boundary values \
from above. The complex radial variable is the package symbol zVar.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"14180578-0550-4db2-a419-c6363e5c13e3"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"fea8de0d-f05e-4739-a40c-dcdb2f5cc242"],

