Cell["Stage 1: the first-order singular mode", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7600abd7-a374-4495-8afa-c30fd67c0662"],

Cell["\<\
psi_p = DSolveValue[L_l psi == deltaExt] /. C[_] -> 0, exactly as in \
Singular-and-regular-split-works-real-outside-worldtube.nb. DSolve writes the \
antiderivatives with Log[r0 - z] and Log[z - r0] (l = 0, 1) or Log[r0 - z] \
and Log[z] (l >= 2). Log[r0 - z] evaluated at real z > r0 with Mathematica's \
principal branch is the value from BELOW; canonicalizeLogs rewrites it as \
Log[z - r0] - I Pi, the same analytic function in the upper half plane.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f8b472ad-4d2e-4b60-9393-df5a1ae07b30"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
